{
  "title": "Clover Club (Raspberry Liqueur)",
  "description": "An eggy, fluffy, raspberry-inflected gin sour, made two ways.",
  "instructions": "Raspberry Syrup:\n\nCombine raspberries and sugar in a saucepan, then muddle the raspberries, releasing the juice into the sugar.\n\nAdd water to the raspberry/sugar mix, then place on a stovetop and set to medium-low heat. Stir to integrate.\n\nContinue to heat and stir until sugar and water are fully integrated, about 10-15 minutes. (You will obviously have raspberry chunks, but you should not be able to scrape a sludge of sugar off the bottom of the saucepan.) Do not let the mixture boil.\n\nTurn off burner. Let cool for 15 minutes, then strain out the berry solids using a fine mesh strainer or cheesecloth.\n\nCool in the refrigerator before using.\n\nStore in the refrigerator after using. It will keep for about a month.\n\nClover Club (Raspberry Liqueur):\n\nCombine all ingredients in a shaker.\n\nDry shake to integrate, about 10 seconds.\n\nOpen the shaker and add ice. Shake again to chill and dilute, another 10-12 seconds.\n\nStrain into a coupe.\n\nGarnish with a fresh raspberry or two.",
